@*
    No data-theme here. Dark is the stylesheet's default and a reader whose system says light gets
    light — pinning the attribute meant a light-preferring reader was served dark regardless, which
    is not "dark is the default", it is "there is one theme".
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
    <Routes />
    @*
        No blazor.web.js. Static server rendering only — every page here is a document, and the
        three places the design allows motion are plain CSS. Adding the script would opt the whole
        site into enhanced navigation and quietly break the no-script guarantee the facet panel
        and plain mode both depend on.
    *@
</body>
</html>
